The `sections` selector in `main.js` `updateActiveNavLink()` already uses `document.querySelectorAll('section[id]')` which dynamically includes new sections — no changes needed there.

### Section L: Accessibility & Keyboard Navigation

These are additions to `index.html` and `main.js`:

1. **Skip link** — First element in `<body>`, before the scroll progress bar:
   ```html
   <a href="#about" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
   ```
   CSS: hidden by default, visible on `:focus`:
   ```css
   .skip-link {
     position: absolute; top: -100%; left: 0;
     background: var(--color-primary); color: #fff;
     padding: 8px 16px; z-index: 9999;
     border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-sm) 0;
   }
   .skip-link:focus { top: 0; }
   ```

2. **Focus-visible rings** — Replace browser default with a styled ring using `--color-accent`:
   ```css
   :focus-visible {
     outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
     outline-offset: 3px;
     border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
   }
   :focus:not(:focus-visible) { outline: none; }
   ```

3. **ARIA labels** — Add `role="main"` to the first non-nav section (or wrap sections in `<main>`). Add `aria-label` to the publications section: `<section aria-labelledby="pub-heading">` and `id="pub-heading"` on the h2.

4. **Filter state** — Publication filter buttons should use `aria-pressed` instead of just a visual `active` class. Update JS to toggle `aria-pressed="true/false"`.

5. **Reduced motion** — Wrap all animations in a media query:
   ```css
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
     *, *::before, *::after {
       animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
       transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
     }
   }
   ```

---

## 4. CSS Architecture Approach

The current single-file approach is correct for a no-build-tool static site. Keep it as one file. The internal structure should be reorganized from top to bottom in this order (with clear comment banners):

```
/* 1. CSS Custom Properties (:root + [data-theme="dark"]) */
/* 2. Reset & Base */
/* 3. Typography Utilities */
/* 4. Layout Utilities (.container, .section, .section-alt) */
/* 5. Buttons */
/* 6. Scroll Progress Bar */
/* 7. Skip Link */
/* 8. Navbar */
/* 9. Hero */
/* 10. About */
/* 11. News */
/* 12. Research / Projects */
/* 13. Timeline / CV */
/* 14. Publications */
/* 15. Contact */
/* 16. Footer */
/* 17. Animations (@keyframes consolidated here) */
/* 18. Accessibility (focus-visible, reduced-motion) */
/* 19. Responsive (mobile-first, ascending breakpoint order: 480, 640, 768, 860, 1100) */
```

**Key CSS principles to apply:**

- All theme-sensitive colors must use CSS variables only — no hardcoded hex values in component rules (the current file has many hardcoded `rgba(29,78,216,...)` values that must be converted to `rgba(var(--color-primary-rgb), ...)` or replaced with token-based approach)
- Glass morphism cards use `backdrop-filter: blur()` with a `@supports` fallback: `@supports not (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) { .news-card { background: var(--color-bg-card); } }`
- Animation performance: use `transform` and `opacity` only for transitions; avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`
- CSS custom property for nav height so all `padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + ...)` references auto-update

---

## 5. JavaScript Enhancements Summary

All JS remains in `js/main.js`. New additions to the existing 85-line file:

| Feature | Lines to Add | Dependencies |
|---------|-------------|--------------|
| Scroll progress bar | ~8 lines | DOM: `#scroll-progress` |
| Theme toggle + persistence | ~20 lines | DOM: `#themeToggle`, `<html data-theme>` |
